WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.920
Do you remember the concepts we studied in
the previous lesson?

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.920
First, we
understood that OPAQUE objects do not allow

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.299
light to pass through them.

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:20.310
Second, TRANSPARENT objects allow light to
pass through them and we can see

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.529
through them clearly.

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:25.900
And third, TRANSLUCENT objects allow light
to pass through

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.869
them partially.

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:31.099
Now I want you to answer this question!

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:34.120
What kind of an object is human body?

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.060
Are we able to see THROUGH it?

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.329
Not really!

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:41.170
Hence a human body is an OPAQUE
object!

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.120
What happens when light is obstructed by the
human body?

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.199
We see that the human body is obstructing
light here!

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:53.750
There is light in front of the
human body but what do you see behind it?

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.129
Yes, a SHADOW.

00:00:56.129 --> 00:00:59.629
This thing you see behind the body is called
a shadow!

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:03.670
Now looking at this, can you tell me the things
that are required for a shadow to

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.839
be formed?

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:06.930
Two things are obvious.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.260
First: a source of light, which is in front
of the body.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.840
And second: an opaque
object… here the human body is the opaque

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.790
object.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:20.280
Can you identify any other thing we may need
for a shadow?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.990
Maybe not.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.090
Now let
us consider a different situation.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.350
[Same person standing in open area against
some natural environment such as

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.350
sea or open fields, but source of light is
low so that shadow is not seen]

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:30.130
In this situation too, we have a source of
light as well as an opaque body.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.970
But, do
we see a shadow?

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.439
NO we don’t.

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:36.009
Do you know why?

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:37.259
Perplexed?

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:41.380
Well, had there been a screen behind the opaque
object, you would

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.490
have seen the shadow on it.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:46.210
But because there is no SCREEN or SURFACE
like in

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.909
the previous case, we cannot see the shadow.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.509
What does this tell us?

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:56.890
It tells us that we also need a SURFACE on
which a shadow can be formed.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.049
That
surface will make us see the shadow!

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:02.909
What’s so special about shadows?

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:06.200
Shadows also give us some information about
the object!

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.370
So if I show you this
shadow, you will be able to tell me that it’s

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:11.730
a human body’s shadow!

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.070
But sometimes they can also be misleading!

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:18.690
For instance, can you name the body
of which this is a shadow?

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:22.670
You’d probably say it’s that of a dog,
but it’s just our

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.590
human hands playing the trick!

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:25.830
3 of 3

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.080
Has it ever occurred to you as to why shadows
are formed?

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.390
We know one of the reasons!

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.140
Opaque bodies do not allow light to pass through
them.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:39.370
Yes that’s one of the main reasons why shadows
are formed!

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.560
Another
important reason for shadows to form is that

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.750
LIGHT TRAVELS IN A STRAIGHT LINE.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.819
We will see its use in our next lesson.

